        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Persistent PTY replaces childprocess for terminal commands",
        "summary": "Terminal command execution in npm-app/src/tool-handlers.ts switched from child_process.spawn to a persistent PTY using @cdktf/node-pty-prebuilt-multiarch. This change unifies stdout and stderr into a single stream to better emulate real terminal behavior and preserve colors, requiring updates to handleRunTerminalCommand return types and CLI output handling in npm-app/src/cli.ts. A resetPtyShell function was added to restart the shell on timeouts or initialization, replacing the previous kill logic. Backend prompt handling in backend/src/main-prompt.ts was also updated to strip STOP_MARKER from printed chunks.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:39:25.028Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the assistant runs commands in your terminal (like running a script or checking files), it used to run them in a way that mixed up the output and error messages separately. Now it uses a real terminal emulator inside, which keeps all the output together, preserves colors and formatting, and behaves more like when you type commands yourself. If you watch the assistant work in a command line, you'll see colors and formatting that were missing before, and commands won't get stuck as often because it can restart the terminal cleanly if something hangs. This is already in effect today for anyone using the assistant through the command-line version.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "10a5109e9457",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:20:50.961Z"
      },
